# KJobs context

Read `docs/CONTEXT.md` before changing behavior. Visual rules are in `FRONTEND-STANDARDS.md`.

Two apps: `kjobs-backend` (Laravel 12, Sanctum, SQLite) and this Next.js 16 app. Roles: `user` (seeker), `employer`, `admin`. Inactive users get 403. Register requires `password_confirmation`. Employer register creates the user and `employer_profiles` in one transaction; `users.name` is the contact person.

Auth is real: NextAuth (`user-credentials`, `employer-credentials`, `admin-credentials`) → Laravel → Sanctum bearer on the JWT (`accessToken`). Public screens are `/login` and `/register`. Legacy `/api/register` and `/api/login` exist but this app does not call them. `/user/login` and `/employer/login` redirect to the public forms.

`src/proxy.ts` gates `/admin`, `/user`, and `/employer`. Do not add `middleware.ts`.

Laravel routes that exist: role register/login, legacy register/login, `/auth/me`, `/auth/logout`, `/admin/login`, `/admin/me`, `/admin/logout`, `GET /admin/users`. No job, application, employer-admin, or dashboard-stats routes. Do not invent them unless asked. Admin screens that call the missing paths already show an unavailable-API message.

Components do not call `fetch`. Use `src/utils/endpoint.ts`, `src/fetch/fetch.ts`, and `src/services/*`. Keep mock signatures (`{ success, message, data }` plus `delay()`).

Mocked (do not hardcode in JSX):

- `public-job-service`, `public-seeker-service` — static data
- `saved-jobs-service`, `user-application-service` — `kjobs.saved-jobs.<userId>`, `kjobs.user-applications.<userId>`
- `employer-portal-service` — `kjobs.employer-jobs`, `kjobs.employer-applications`
- `contact-service` — validates and returns success, stores nothing

Do not "fix" these quietly:

- DB application status is `applied | reviewing | shortlisted | rejected | hired`. Frontend enums say `pending | reviewed`. Jobs also have `draft`.
- `EmployerProfile::jobs()` points at a missing `Job` model. The model is `JobListing`.
- `GET /api/admin/users` already filters `role = user`, then applies `role` again, so an employer/admin query returns nothing.
- `isAdminAuthPath` treats `/forgot-password` as an admin auth path. That page is public.

Leave `src/app/(pages)/admin/**` and `src/components/admin-*` alone unless the task is admin. Tailwind only. Shared `src/components/ui` is used by admin.

Ignore leftover template files (`meal`, `school`, `subscription*`, `course-module`, `billing-invoice`, `types/school.ts`, WellSnax images).
